WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:01.650
OK.

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:06.590
We literally have seen people argue that it
is OK to crowd together in houses of worship

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:12.150
churches because Jesus is protecting the people
from Corona virus.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.780
Remember this lady a couple of months ago,
six weeks ago, driving out of this Ohio parking

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:21.880
lot is a woman who just attended a church
service with dozens of other people, including

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:22.880
children.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.510
May I ask you about your decision to go to
church, to be inside that building?

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:27.230
I wouldn't be anywhere else.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:30.800
Aren't you concerned you could infect other
people if you get sick inside?

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.240
Now, a little.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.680
Now I'm covered in Jesus blood.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.230
I'm covered in blood.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:39.780
Other people who don't go to this church who
you might encounter, all these people go to

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:49.380
this church, but you're going to be in places
where other crashes every day.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.380
I'm so sick from what happened because I'm
covered in blood.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:51.800
Thank you very much.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:58.510
It turns out not only was that not true, but
churches, while trying to get coronavirus

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:04.170
stimulus money, are often staying open, causing
new outbreaks of disease.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:10.570
New York Pastor Fabian Arius has a parish
that lost 44 people to Corona virus.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.420
That's not cases.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.930
Forty four deaths to Corona virus Bishop Paul
Eggan.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:22.180
Steinar, from an Evangelical Lutheran Church
network, says that the pastors in their network

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:28.190
are reporting in some cases, 25 to 50 percent
of their congregations have Corona virus in

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:30.740
the south of the United States.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:35.030
We've seen more of these huge evangelical
churches stay open.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.060
And there's a whole bunch of examples, Kentucky.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:42.820
There was an outbreak that started and then
moved from the church to g.e.'s aviation plant

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:44.350
in Madisonville.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:49.290
70 infections have been traced back to a church
in Sacramento, California.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:54.530
The full list is not so important, but the
point is churches have been huge epicenters

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:55.979
of outbreaks.

00:01:55.979 --> 00:01:58.580
Some churches not all, to be super clear.

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:04.310
Some churches have been the loudest advocates
against the stay at home orders, wanting exemptions

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.940
from the large gathering bans, for example.

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:09.700
And yet, at the same time, they want coronavirus
money.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:15.019
Houses of worship have received hundreds of
millions, certainly maybe even billions of

00:02:15.019 --> 00:02:17.269
dollars under the paycheck protection plan.

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:22.359
And the reason is because churches are being
treated like any business or nonprofit that

00:02:22.359 --> 00:02:23.359
needs funding.

00:02:23.359 --> 00:02:25.510
So understand the hypocrisy here.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:29.040
Churches want to be exempt from stay at home
orders because they say we're not like any

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.189
other business or organization.

00:02:31.189 --> 00:02:35.849
But they say we are just like any other business
organization when it comes to peopIe funds.

00:02:35.849 --> 00:02:38.159
Now, the truth is more complex.

00:02:38.159 --> 00:02:43.989
Many of the churches that are seeking funds
have shut down or are doing only online stuff.

00:02:43.989 --> 00:02:47.499
Many churches in Massachusetts, for example,
fall under that umbrella.

00:02:47.499 --> 00:02:52.209
So I am not individually saying every church
is hip.

00:02:52.209 --> 00:02:56.319
Critical because they are all against shut
downs and all taking BPP money.

00:02:56.319 --> 00:02:57.489
That's not the case.

00:02:57.489 --> 00:03:03.029
Many of the churches that got BPP funds are
Catholic churches and many Catholic churches

00:03:03.029 --> 00:03:06.150
have been closing in accordance with state
guidelines.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:11.109
But the special treatment has to stop guys
in the eyes of the law and under government.

00:03:11.109 --> 00:03:16.730
We've already said churches likely shouldn't
be non-profits and churches probably should

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.410
be paying property taxes.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:25.290
Now I have no problem if the church has a
school or a daycare, something that is truly

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.109
a traditional standard nonprofit.

00:03:28.109 --> 00:03:34.870
I'm fine looking at exemptions there, but
the general blanket idea that by saying you

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:37.309
are a place of worship, you pay no taxes.

00:03:37.309 --> 00:03:38.309
It has to end.

00:03:38.309 --> 00:03:42.209
And in addition, in exchange for the privilege
of not paying taxes.

00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:45.689
Houses of worship are not supposed to be political,
and often they are.

00:03:45.689 --> 00:03:47.419
Rarely are there ever repercussions.

00:03:47.419 --> 00:03:49.760
So I just want consistency.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:53.739
If you want to be treated just like any other
business and get your peopIe money and all

00:03:53.739 --> 00:04:00.450
of that, well then you don't get to say we
are different and we get to stay open as as

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:02.389
if we were an essential business.

00:04:02.389 --> 00:04:03.980
Why would that be the case?

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:10.139
If you are special and you get to stay open
no matter what and you get to not pay taxes?

00:04:10.139 --> 00:04:13.559
Why do you also get the peopIe funds?

00:04:13.559 --> 00:04:17.310
And then more urgently, because really, you
know, I care more about lives than the money

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.510
component.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.680
The issue of funding, taxes, all of that.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.759
It's important, but it's not urgent.

00:04:22.759 --> 00:04:28.710
The issue of churches as a locus for coronavirus
outbreaks, that is both important and urgent.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:29.870
Very much so.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:31.880
And I don't know at this point what can be
done.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:38.590
There are actually churches that are deliberately
being defiant when it comes to coronavirus

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:39.729
and staying open.

00:04:39.729 --> 00:04:43.199
And it has to stop because it's spreading
infection and as a result it is spreading

00:04:43.199 --> 00:05:55.770
death.

